# Line endings are LF in the repository, always.
#
# Without this, `prettier --write .` on Windows rewrote every file it touched from LF to
# CRLF, and `git status` then showed forty files as modified with zero content changes.
# That is not cosmetic: the closeout review of 2026-09-06 already named whole-repo
# formatting churn in the same tree as logic changes as the thing that hides a review.
# A diff nobody can read is a review nobody performs.
#
# Checkout is normalised too (no `eol=crlf` for Windows): every tool in this repo —
# node, prettier, astro — handles LF on Windows, and one convention beats two.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ico binary

# The ICS endpoint emits CRLF because RFC 5545 requires it. The generated file never
# reaches git (dist/ is ignored), but the fixture strings in the test do — and a test
# that asserts CRLF must not have its own source rewritten.
*.ics -text
